# Space Analyzer Pro - AI Agent Rules

## After Every Code Change
- Run `just verify` to check formatting, linting, and tests pass

## Never Modify
- Files in `archive/` - historical reference only
- `config/secrets/` - contains sensitive configuration
- `.env` files - never commit secrets

## Code Style
- Rust: follow rustfmt.toml settings, pass `cargo clippy --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings`
- Format with `cargo fmt --all`
- Use `thiserror` for error types, `anyhow` for application-level handling
- Document public items with `///` doc comments

## Commit Convention
- Use conventional commits: `feat(scope): description`
- Scopes: `gui`, `scanner`, `ai`, `native`, `shared`, `gpu`, `docs`, `test`

## Project Structure
- This is a **Rust desktop application** (egui/eframe GUI)
- Core source: `src/` (GUI, Ollama client, database, workflows)
- Native modules: `native/` (scanner, deduplicator, node_modules_cleaner)
- Shared crates: `shared-scanner/`, `gpu-compute/`
- See `AGENTS.md` for full directory map
